  "text": "[NRTM.5.2] The INIT→LIVE transition is the public call **`ds_engine_go_live`**. It is **one-way** and MUST be called after `ds_engine_set_wm_max`\n(which sizes the pools and locks the intern table) and after the bundle is\nloaded and warmed — every string the workload uses must be interned before the\nlock. After it returns `DS_OK` the pump runs zero-alloc under the loaded\ncontract. The board runtimes (under `runtime/esp32*`, `runtime/rp2350`,\n`runtime/samd51`, …) call it as part of bring-up, so a board integration rarely\ninvokes it directly; a custom or bare-metal port calls it itself.\n\n",
